## Lore

The Consortium Armed Forces Trooper is the everyday space soldier of the
Consortium of Civilized Worlds, roughly what a Coalition grunt is to Rifts
Earth. Troopers train for ground combat and space combat alike, and the job is
as much policing as fighting: they serve as military police and peacekeepers,
hold security aboard starships and space stations, and patrol the spaceways of
CCW territory.

The CAF is the largest military in the Three Galaxies and a trooper''s posting
can be anywhere in it, which is why the language training is as heavy as the
weapons training. A trooper who cannot make himself understood on a Gateland
dock is no use to the Consortium.

## Pay and posting

Standard salary is 2,000 credits a month on top of the starting savings.
Cybernetics are none to start with, and are likely to stay that way: most
cultures of the Three Galaxies view cybernetic and bionic replacements with
distaste and avoid them where they can.

## GM Notes

The trooper is the book''s baseline soldier and the class every other CAF entry
is measured against. The CAF Officers Corps - the rear-echelon officers who did
not graduate into Fleet Command - are explicitly run as CAF Troopers rather than
as CAF Fleet Officers (printed 58).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'caf-trooper');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'caf-trooper';

